peedy{background-color:#310402}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .ambox-speedy{background-color:#310402}}</style></span><table class="box-More_citations_needed plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-content ambox-Refimprove" role="presentation" about="#mwt2"><tbody><tr><td class="mbox-image"><div class="mbox-image-div"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Question_book-new.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Question_book-new.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/99/Question_book-new.svg/60px-Question_book-new.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/99/Question_book-new.svg/120px-Question_book-new.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="icon" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="399" data-file-type="drawing" height="39" width="50" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div></td><td class="mbox-text"><div class="mbox-text-span">This article <b>needs <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability">more citations</a></b>.<span class="hide-when-compact"> Please help <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/31_equal_temperament" title="Special:EditPage/31 equal temperament">improve this article</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Referencing_for_beginners" title="Help:Referencing for beginners">adding citations to reliable sources</a>. Unsourced material may be challenged and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Burden_of_evidence" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability">removed</a>.<br/><small><span class="plainlinks"><i>Find sources:</i><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/search?as_eq=wikipedia&amp;q=%2231+equal+temperament%22" class="external text">"31 equal temperament"</a><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>–<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/search?tbm=nws&amp;q=%2231+equal+temperament%22+-wikipedia&amp;tbs=ar:1" class="external text">news</a> <b>·</b> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/search?&amp;q=%2231+equal+temperament%22&amp;tbs=bkt:s&amp;tbm=bks" class="external text">newspapers</a> <b>·</b> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/search?tbs=bks:1&amp;q=%2231+equal+temperament%22+-wikipedia" class="external text">books</a> <b>·</b> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=%2231+equal+temperament%22" class="external text">scholar</a> <b>·</b> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstor.org/action/doBasicSearch?Query=%2231+equal+temperament%22&amp;acc=on&amp;wc=on" class="external text">JSTOR</a></span></small></span>  <span class="date-container"><i>(<span class="date">July 2024</span>)</i></span><span class="hide-when-compact"><i> (<small><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal" title="Help:Maintenance template removal">Learn how and when to remove this message</a></small>)</i></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_needing_additional_references_from_July_2024"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_needing_additional_references"/></span>
<p class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwBA"><span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4" id="mwBQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"use dmy dates","href":"./Template:Use_dmy_dates"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"November 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Use_dmy_dates_from_November_2024" about="#mwt4" id="mwBg"/></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg/250px-Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg/500px-Syntonic_tuning_continuum.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="290" data-file-height="710" data-file-type="drawing" height="612" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCg"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt5" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r920966791" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt6" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output span.smallcaps{font-variant:small-caps}.mw-parser-output span.smallcaps-smaller{font-size:85%}</style><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span> on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_diatonic_tuning" title="Regular diatonic tuning" id="mwDA">regular diatonic tuning</a> continuum at <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt7" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"[[perfect fifth|p5]] {{=}} 696.77&amp;nbsp;[[cents (music)|cents]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfect_fifth" title="Perfect fifth">p5</a> = 696.77<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cents_(music)" title="Cents (music)" class="mw-redirect">cents</a></span><sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Milne-Sethares-Plamondon-2007_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Milne-Sethares-Plamondon-2007"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Milne-Sethares-Plamondon-2007-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Milne-Sethares-Plamondon-2007-1" id="mwDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwEg">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music" title="Music" id="mwEw">music</a>, <b id="mwFA">31 equal temperament</b>, <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt11" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" 31 {{sc|ET}},"}},"i":0}}]}'> 31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt12" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">ET</span>,</span> which can also be abbreviated  <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt13" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" 31 {{sc|TET}}"}},"i":0}}]}'> 31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">TET</span></span> (31<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFw"> </span>tone <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt15" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwGA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sc","href":"./Template:Sc"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ET"}},"i":0}}]}'/><span class="smallcaps " about="#mwt15" id="mwGQ">ET</span>) or <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt17" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwGg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 [[equal division of the octave|{{sc|EDO}}]]"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equal_division_of_the_octave" title="Equal division of the octave" class="mw-redirect"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></a></span> (equal division of the octave), also known as <b id="mwGw">tricesimoprimal</b>, is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musical_temperament" title="Musical temperament" id="mwHA">tempered</a> scale derived by dividing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octave" title="Octave" id="mwHQ">octave</a> into 31<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwHg"> </span>equally-proportioned steps (equal frequency ratios). <span class="ext-phonos" typeof="mw:Extension/phonos mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt19" id="mwHw" data-mw='{"name":"phonos","attrs":{"file":"31-tet scale on C.mid"},"body":{"extsrc":"Play"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"audio","href":"./Template:Audio"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31-tet scale on C.mid"},"2":{"wt":"Play"}},"i":0}}]}'><span data-nosnippet="" id="ooui-php-1" class="noexcerpt ext-phonos-PhonosButton oo-ui-widget oo-ui-widget-enabled oo-ui-buttonElement oo-ui-buttonElement-frameless oo-ui-buttonElement-size-medium oo-ui-iconElement oo-ui-labelElement oo-ui-buttonWidget" data-ooui='{"_":"mw.Phonos.PhonosButton","href":"\/\/upload.wikimedia.org\/wikipedia\/commons\/transcoded\/1\/1c\/31-tet_scale_on_C.mid\/31-tet_scale_on_C.mid.mp3","rel":["nofollow"],"framed":false,"icon":"volumeUp","label":{"html":"Play"},"data":{"ipa":"","text":"","lang":"en","wikibase":"","file":"31-tet scale on C.mid"},"classes":["noexcerpt","ext-phonos-PhonosButton"]}'><a role="button" tabindex="0" href="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1c/31-tet_scale_on_C.mid/31-tet_scale_on_C.mid.mp3" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Play audio" title="Play audio" class="oo-ui-buttonElement-button"><span class="oo-ui-iconElement-icon oo-ui-icon-volumeUp"></span><span class="oo-ui-labelElement-label">Play</span><span class="oo-ui-indicatorElement-indicator oo-ui-indicatorElement-noIndicator"></span></a></span><sup class="ext-phonos-attribution noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable"><a href="/wiki/File:31-tet_scale_on_C.mid" title="File:31-tet scale on C.mid">ⓘ</a></sup></span> Each step represents a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frequency" title="Frequency" id="mwIA">frequency</a> ratio of <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt21" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"radic","href":"./Template:Radic"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2 "},"2":{"wt":"31"}},"i":0}}]}'><sup style="margin-right: -0.5em; vertical-align: 0.8em;">31</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity">√</span><span style="border-top:1px solid; padding:0 0.1em;">2 </span></span>, or 38.71<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwIg"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cent_(music)" title="Cent (music)" id="mwIw">cents</a> (<span class="ext-phonos" typeof="mw:Extension/phonos mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt22" id="mwJA" data-mw='{"name":"phonos","attrs":{"file":"1 step in 31-et on C.mid"},"body":{"extsrc":"Play"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Audio","href":"./Template:Audio"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1 step in 31-et on C.mid"},"2":{"wt":"Play"}},"i":0}}]}'><span data-nosnippet="" id="ooui-php-2" class="noexcerpt ext-phonos-PhonosButton oo-ui-widget oo-ui-widget-enabled oo-ui-buttonElement oo-ui-buttonElement-frameless oo-ui-buttonElement-size-medium oo-ui-iconElement oo-ui-labelElement oo-ui-buttonWidget" data-ooui='{"_":"mw.Phonos.PhonosButton","href":"\/\/upload.wikimedia.org\/wikipedia\/commons\/transcoded\/9\/94\/1_step_in_31-et_on_C.mid\/1_step_in_31-et_on_C.mid.mp3","rel":["nofollow"],"framed":false,"icon":"volumeUp","label":{"html":"Play"},"data":{"ipa":"","text":"","lang":"en","wikibase":"","file":"1 step in 31-et on C.mid"},"classes":["noexcerpt","ext-phonos-PhonosButton"]}'><a role="button" tabindex="0" href="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/94/1_step_in_31-et_on_C.mid/1_step_in_31-et_on_C.mid.mp3" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Play audio" title="Play audio" class="oo-ui-buttonElement-button"><span class="oo-ui-iconElement-icon oo-ui-icon-volumeUp"></span><span class="oo-ui-labelElement-label">Play</span><span class="oo-ui-indicatorElement-indicator oo-ui-indicatorElement-noIndicator"></span></a></span><sup class="ext-phonos-attribution noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable"><a href="/wiki/File:1_step_in_31-et_on_C.mid" title="File:1 step in 31-et on C.mid">ⓘ</a></sup></span>).</p>

<p id="mwJQ"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt24" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt25" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span> is often thought to be a very accurate approximation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarter-comma_meantone" title="Quarter-comma meantone" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJw">quarter-comma meantone</a> temperament. More generally, it is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_diatonic_tuning" title="Regular diatonic tuning" id="mwKA">regular diatonic tuning</a> in which the tempered perfect fifth is equal to 696.77<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwKQ"> </span>cents, as shown in Figure<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwKg"> </span>1. On an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isomorphic_keyboard" title="Isomorphic keyboard" id="mwKw">isomorphic keyboard</a>, the fingering of music composed in <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt26" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt27" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span> is precisely the same as it is in any other syntonic tuning (such as <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt28" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"[[12 equal temperament|12 {{sc|EDO}}]]),"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/12_equal_temperament" title="12 equal temperament" class="mw-redirect">12 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt29" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></a>),</span> so long as the notes are spelled properly—that is, with no assumption of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enharmonic" title="Enharmonic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLg">enharmonicity</a>.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwLw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwMA" aria-labelledby="History_and_use"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History_and_use">History and use</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=31_equal_temperament&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History and use"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwMQ">Division of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octave" title="Octave" id="mwMg">octave</a> into 31<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwMw"> </span>steps arose naturally out of Renaissance <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_theory" title="Music theory" id="mwNA">music theory</a>; the lesser <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesis" title="Diesis" id="mwNQ">diesis</a><span style="visibility:hidden; color:transparent; padding-left:2px" about="#mwt30" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"px2","href":"./Template:Px2"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity">‍</span></span> – the ratio of an octave to three major thirds, 128:125 or 41.06<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwNw"> </span>cents – was approximately one-fifth of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_second" title="Major second" id="mwOA">tone</a> or two-fifths of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semitone" title="Semitone" id="mwOQ">semitone</a>. In 1555, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicola_Vicentino" title="Nicola Vicentino" id="mwOg">Nicola Vicentino</a> proposed an extended-meantone tuning of 31<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwOw"> </span>tones. In 1666, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemme_Rossi" title="Lemme Rossi" id="mwPA">Lemme Rossi</a> first proposed an equal temperament of this order. In 1691, having discovered it independently, scientist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christiaan_Huygens" title="Christiaan Huygens" id="mwPQ">Christiaan Huygens</a> wrote about it also.<sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_lacking_reliable_references" about="#mwt31" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwQg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unreliable source","href":"./Template:Unreliable_source"},"params":{"failed":{"wt":"y"},"date":{"wt":"July 2026"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_lacking_reliable_references_from_July_2026" about="#mwt31"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt31" id="mwQw"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Reliable_sources" title="Wikipedia:Reliable sources"><span title="The material near this tag relies on an unreliable source. (July 2026)">unreliable source</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup>
Since the standard system of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musical_tuning" title="Musical tuning" id="mwRA">tuning</a> at that time was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarter-comma_meantone" title="Quarter-comma meantone" class="mw-redirect" id="mwRQ">quarter-comma meantone</a>, in which the fifth is tuned to <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt35" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"radic","href":"./Template:Radic"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"5 "},"2":{"wt":"4"}},"i":0}}]}'><sup style="margin-right: -0.5em; vertical-align: 0.8em;">4</sup><span typeof="mw:Entity">√</span><span style="border-top:1px solid; padding:0 0.1em;">5 </span></span>, the appeal of this method was immediate, as the fifth of <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt36" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwRw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt37" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span>, at 696.77<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwSA"> </span>cents, is very slightly closer to a true 2:3 interval than the fifth of quarter-comma meantone. Huygens not only realized this, he went farther and noted that <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt38" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwSQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt39" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span> provides an excellent approximation of septimal, or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limit_(music)" title="Limit (music)" id="mwSg">7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwSw"> </span>limit</a> harmony.</p>

<p id="mwTA">In the twentieth century, physicist, music theorist, and composer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adriaan_Fokker" title="Adriaan Fokker" id="mwTQ">Adriaan Fokker</a>, after reading Huygens's work, led a revival of interest in this system of tuning which led to a number of compositions, particularly by Dutch composers. Fokker designed the Fokker organ, a 31<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwTg"> </span>tone equal-tempered organ, which was installed in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teyler's_Museum" title="Teyler's Museum" class="mw-redirect" id="mwTw">Teyler's Museum</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haarlem" title="Haarlem" id="mwUA">Haarlem</a> in 1951 and moved to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muziekgebouw_aan_'t_IJ" title="Muziekgebouw aan 't IJ" id="mwUQ">Muziekgebouw aan 't IJ</a> in 2010 where it has been frequently used in concerts since it moved.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwUg" aria-labelledby="Interval_size"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Interval_size">Interval size</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=31_equal_temperament&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Interval size"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwUw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:31ed2.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwVA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:31ed2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/31ed2.svg/250px-31ed2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/31ed2.svg/500px-31ed2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="500" data-file-height="1670" data-file-type="drawing" height="835" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwVQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwVg"> 19<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwVw"> </span>limit just intonation intervals approximated in <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt40" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwWA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nobr","href":"./Template:Nobr"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"31 {{sc|EDO}}"}},"i":0}}]}'>31 <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r920966791" about="#mwt41" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"smallcaps/styles.css"}}'/><span class="smallcaps ">EDO</span></span> </figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwWQ">Here are the sizes of some common intervals:</p>

